// REJECTS: PLACEHOLDER
//
// `sink:` is Relational{database} XOR ObjectStorage{binding}. The two sub-rules are
// `(sinkDatabase)*` and `(sinkBinding)*` -- each accepts an EMPTY body, so a sink with
// neither field parses and is caught by the walker, but a sink with the OTHER field is
// caught by the grammar. This file is the second case: an object-storage binding under a
// relational sink.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::RelationalSinkWithBinding
{
  doc: 'relational sink given an object storage binding';
  trigger: Manual;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  persister: Batch
  {
    sink: Relational
    {
      binding: test::persistence::Binding;
    }
    ingestMode: NontemporalSnapshot
    {
      auditing: None;
    }
    targetShape: Flat
    {
      modelClass: test::persistence::ModelClass;
      targetName: 'TestDataset1';
    }
  }
}
